hey all

a reasonably straightforward  use of plyr, when you have a data set where durations' start and conclusion are encoded in variables. consider:

d1 <- data.frame(indiv = 1:2,
                 start = c(2002, 2006),
                 end = c(2008, 2009))
> >d1
>   indiv start  end
> 1     1  2002 2008
> 2     2  2006 2009

if I wanted  to make each row a person.year, the plyr syntax is trival

head(ddply(d1, .(indiv), function(i) data.frame(years = seq(i$start, i$end, 1))))

> indiv years
> 1     1  2002
> 2     1  2003
> 3     1  2004
> 4     1  2005
> 5     1  2006
> 6     1  2007

but translating this to dplyr eludes me. both of these fail:

tbl_df(d1) %>%
    group_by(indiv) %>%
    data.frame(years = seq(start, end, 1))

tbl_df(d1) %>%
    group_by(indiv) %>%
    summarize(years = seq(start, end, 1))

how can you do this in dplyr?

